    {
      "id": "claim_142274db2b144235a713ce3aa8d9547e",
      "statement": "ArchitectureTest structurally guards cache-key completeness: every concrete CacheKey implementation must expose a static of(CacheParameter, String) factory whose body calls every attribute accessor of its CacheParameter (excluding parameters(), createCacheKey(), and equals/hashCode/toString), and every CacheParameter implementation's parameters() must access all of its non-static fields, because an unread attribute would make different configurations collide on cache entries or cache files and silently return wrong cached results.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/test/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/llm/ArchitectureTest.java#L18-L40",
